<title>GERMANY: Deutsche completes takeover of Grunelius.</title>
<headline>Deutsche completes takeover of Grunelius.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's largest bank Deutsche Bank AG said on Wednesday that it had upped its stake in the private banking group Grunelius to 100 percent, from 84 percent previously.</p>
<p>Deutsche Bank Management board member Tessen von Heydebreck said the increase in its Grunelius stake would have effect from December 31 1996.</p>
<p>Deutsche said Grunelius would be used to focus on Deutsche's private customer business and the bank said it would be generating new jobs in this area.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
